Others deities were added from the [[Shrine Consolidation Policy]] including. See this page for the source shrines for each deity.<ref name=":0" /> {| class="wikitable" |+ !Deity !domain |- |[[Amaterasu]] |Sun goddess |- |[[Hachiman]] ([[Emperor Ōjin|Emperor Ojin]], '''品陀和気命)''' |God of victory |- |[[Tenjin]] ([[Sugawara no Michizane]]) |God of learning and writing |- |[[Ame-no-Tajikarao]] |God of martial arts and power |- |[[Inari Okami]] ({{ill|Ukemochi|en}}) |God of food and cooking |- |[[Susanoo]] ([[Gion worship]]) |God of agriculture, cultivation, and love |- |{{ill|Ame-no-Koyane|en}} ({{Ill|Kasuga Gongen|ja|春日権現|en:draft|Kasuga Gongen|simple|User:Immanuelle/Kasuga no Kami}}) |God of words and music |- |{{ill|Takuhadachiji-hime|en}} |God of clothing and textiles |- |[[Sukunabikona]] |God of alcohol and medicine |- |[[Izanami]] |Goddess of safe delivery and fire suppression |- |{{ill|Ichikishimahime|lt=Sayori-hime no Mikoto|ja|イチキシマヒメ|en}} |Goddess of water and waterway safety |- |{{ill|Takemikazuchi|en}} |God of protection |- |{{ill|Futsunushi|en}} |God of protection |- |{{Ill|Mikumari|ja|水分神|en:draft|Ame-no-mikumari-no-kami|simple|User:Immanuelle/Ame-no-mikumari-no-kami}} |Goddess of water |- |[[Kotoshironushi]] |God of business |- |{{ill|Himegami|lt=Hime Okami|en}} ({{Ill|Kasuga Gongen|ja|春日権現|en:draft|Kasuga Gongen|simple|User:Immanuelle/Kasuga no Kami}}) |{{ill|Ame-no-Koyane|en}}'s wife |- |{{ill|Agata no Inukai no Michiyo|lt=Inukai no Sukune|en}} |Mother of {{ill|Tachibana no Moroe|en}} |}
== history == The year this shrine was founded is unknown, but it is also mentioned in [[Engishiki|the Engishiki]], which was created during [[Heian period|the Heian period]] . In the newly compiled surname register compiled in the early Heian period, there is a description that ``Yagizō, son of Wadasin Toyotama no Mikoto, after Furutama no Mikoto,<nowiki>''</nowiki> indicates that the Yagi clan, an ancient powerful clan, enshrined their ancestral deity, Furutama no Mikoto. It is said that it originated from {{Sfn|岸和田市観光振興協会|1993}} . It used to be the village shrine of Yagigo, but when village shrines were established in each village during [[Edo period|the Edo period]], it was revered as {{Sfn|岸和田市観光振興協会|1993}} village shrine of Nakai Village. is said to be a corruption of ``Nakayagi<nowiki>''</nowiki> {{Sfn|大阪府神道青年会|1971}} ). Afterwards, in [[1872]] ( [[Meiji period|Meiji]] 5) in the Meiji era, it was ranked as a village shrine, and from [[1908]] to [[1909|1909,]] Yagi village, Kitakashimori village Oaza Yoshii, [[Tadaoka, Osaka|Tadaoka village]] Oaza Kitade・The Takatsuki Village Shrine was enshrined {{Sfn|岸和田市観光振興協会|1993}} . It was promoted to Gosha in [[1943]] ( [[Shōwa period|Showa]] 18). {{Sfn|大阪府神道青年会|1971}}
== cultural assets ==
* Kishiwada City designated tangible cultural property ** Ema for rain (by Tsuda Unkei) <ref name="kishiwada">[https://www.city.kishiwada.osaka.jp/soshiki/70/sitei-bunkazai2015.html 岸和田市内の指定文化財一覧] 岸和田市ホームページ 2016年5月13日閲覧。</ref> * Kishiwada City designated natural monument ** Yagi Shrine shrine complex <ref name="kishiwada"></ref>
== Annual festival etc. ==
* Regular festival: [[October 5|October 5th]] every year * Danjiri shrine entrance: Two days before Sports Day every year ** From 8:30 to 9:30 on the first day of the Yagi Danjiri Festival, the Yagi district (Nakai Town, Yoshii Town, Araki Town, Shimoikeda Town, Minodoji Town, Nishioji Town, Komatsato Town, Nukamachi, Nukahara Town, There are 11 Danjiri floats from Omachi, Ikejiri Town). The order of entering the shrine is the same every year. {{Sfn|岸和田市観光振興協会|1993}}
